 "answers": {
  "Q1": "See q1_answers_test.csv: '*' marks Holm-significant skill on the locked test block. Direction skill supported for 2/4 horizons (CV), 0/4 (NLP panel); fusion beat the better single modality in 6/12 tasks.",
  "Q2": "Validation-chosen best CV model: vit_b16_ft (validation mean rank 2.17); on test it ranks 3 of 7; best on test ex post: swin_t_ft. **ViT-B/16** has the best mean rank (2.17) over the 12 validation tasks. Direction (3-class): mean macro_f1 0.330 (behind the best other model on that target by 0.011 on average). Volatility (log RV): mean r2 -0.065 (ahead of the best other model on that target by 0.011 on average). Drawdown > 10%: mean auc 0.513 (behind the best other model on that target by 0.023 on average). Fine-tuning changed its mean primary metric by +0.030 versus its frozen features, so most of its edge comes from adapting to charts. Size: 86.99 M parameters, 5.36 training minutes. Caution: validation was also used to choose it, so its validation lead is optimistic; \u00a723 gives the unbiased test result.",
  "Q3": "Best combination on validation: vit_b16; see cv_combos_test.csv for its test standing and all 63 combinations.",
  "Q4": "Best per target and horizon (validation choice and its test score): cv_best_per_target_test.csv.",
  "Q5": "Best model per sector: cv_best_by_sector_test.csv; interaction test (H6) p-values: dir 0.075, vol 0.015, dd 0.005",
  "Q6": "Reaction size by form (test): 10-K |z| 1.52, 10-Q |z| 1.64, 8-K |z| 1.37, no filing (control) |z| 0.70",
  "Q7": "Sector x form excess reaction over non-filing days: event_study_sector_form_test.csv (development: event_study_sector_form_dev.csv).",
  "Q8": "8-K items ranked by reaction (event_study_8k_items_*.csv), n-grams (nlp_words_*.csv), FinBERT tone (nlp_tone_vs_reaction_dev.csv), attributions (nlp_integrated_gradients_val.csv).",
  "Q9": "Same tables as Q7, read row by row: a sector is 'sensitive' to a form when its excess |z| CI is above zero in both development and test.",
  "Q10": "Top-3 CV + top-3 NLP minus top-3 CV: supported in 3/12 tasks after Holm."
